## Brief Overview

---

The honest planning timeline for an AV rental with MEG is not a countdown, it is a short sequence of decisions. Settle on your expected guest count, which points you to a package. Tell us your date, location and package interest so we can quote it. Clear the 24 hour minimum notice that governs every booking and every change to one. Package price does not move with how far ahead you book, and only 2 packages in the whole catalog come with a technician. Those facts, not a week count, are what actually shape when to reach out.

## Key Highlights

---

-   There is no calendar based lead time table. Guest count and package fit is the first real decision, not a date on a calendar.
-   Package price is fixed: Eco Pack 290 euros, Basic MICE Pack 295 euros, Product Presentation Pack 310 euros, MICE Pack 490 euros, Wedding Pack 650 euros, all ex VAT, regardless of how many weeks or months out you book.
-   Only the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) and [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) include a live technician catalog wide, the MICE Pack for up to 6 continuous hours. Every other package is self run after our crew installs and tests it.
-   The only universal deadline is the 24 hour minimum notice, and it applies equally to a first booking and to a change requested afterward.
-   MEG operates delivery only. Our crew delivers, installs, tests and collects, so there is no self pickup step to plan a buffer around.

## The First Real Decision: Guest Count and Package Fit

<InlineCTA />

Most planning guides start with a date. We start with a headcount, because that is what actually determines which package fits, and each package has a real capacity built into it: the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) covers up to 50 guests self run, the [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) up to 40 self run, the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) up to 80 with a technician throughout, and the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) up to 120 with a technician for up to 6 continuous hours. The [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/) has no fixed guest cap, since it is sized around a screen and a speaker pair rather than a room count.

Getting this right before you book matters more than picking a date far enough in advance, because a guest count that grows past a package's capacity after booking is a switch to a different, higher capacity package, not a quantity you add to. That switch depends on whether the larger system, and on the Wedding Pack or MICE Pack a technician, is still free for your date, which is exactly the kind of thing that is easier to confirm early than to fix late.

## What We Need From You to Build an Accurate Quote

The actual bottleneck in any AV rental timeline is not a countdown, it is whether we have enough to quote you accurately on the first pass. Our process is 4 steps: pick a package, request a quote through our inquiry form, our team contacts you to finalize details and confirm the booking, then we handle delivery, setup, configuration and teardown. To move through steps 2 and 3 quickly, share your event date, the venue location, your expected guest count, and which package interests you. Those 4 details are what let us confirm equipment and, where relevant, technician availability in one exchange rather than several rounds of back and forth.

## The One Hard Deadline: 24 Hours, Not a Suggested Lead Time

Every booking, and every change to one, needs a minimum of 24 hours notice to guarantee scheduling and logistical availability. That is the one rule we actually enforce, and it does not stop applying once you have already booked: a bigger guest count, an added microphone, extra technician hours on the MICE Pack, still needs to clear that same 24 hour window before we can confirm it. Nothing about it gets stricter or softer depending on how far out your event is, which is exactly why we do not publish a separate lead time table for large events versus small ones. The window is the same either way. What changes is how much runway you leave yourself to react if a date or an add on request is not available.

## What Does Not Change However Early or Late You Book

Some guides suggest booking early gets you a better rate. With MEG it does not: every package on our list carries one flat, ex VAT price, and there is no lead time discount or last minute surcharge built into any of them. Booking further ahead protects availability, particularly for the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) and [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) technician slots during busier stretches of the year, it does not change what you pay. If your guest count drops after booking, the price you already confirmed does not drop with it either, since the package, not a per guest rate, is what you are booking.

