## Booking Across the Costa del Sol, Sevilla and Granada

Location is one of the 4 details we ask for precisely because it changes the logistics, not the notice window. Within the Costa del Sol, Malaga capital, Marbella, Coin, Ronda, Mijas, Nerja, Torremolinos, Fuengirola, Benalmadena and Estepona, there is no special minimum. Sevilla is also served. Granada, being out of province, typically requires a rental value over 400 euros to cover the single day travel, which is worth knowing when you are sizing a package for a Granada event, though the same 24 hour minimum notice applies there too, not a longer one.

## Conclusion

The real planning timeline for an audio visual rental in Malaga is 3 things, not a week count: settle your guest count against a package's real capacity, give us your date, location, guest count and package interest so we can quote it in one pass, and clear the 24 hour minimum that governs any booking or change to one. Price does not move with how far ahead you book. [Contact us](/contact/) with those details, and for the full catalog behind this page, see the [audio visual rental in Malaga](/blog/audio-visual-rental/) guide.

## FAQs

### How far in advance should I book audio visual rental in Malaga?

There is no fixed rule or calendar table. What actually matters is confirming your guest count against a package's real capacity, and reaching out early enough that the equipment, and a technician if your package includes one, is still free for your date. See [The First Real Decision](#the-first-real-decision-guest-count-and-package-fit) above.

### Does booking earlier get me a better price?

No. Every package carries one flat, ex VAT price regardless of how far ahead you book. Booking earlier protects availability, particularly for the technician included with the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) and [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), it does not lower what you pay. See [What Does Not Change](#what-does-not-change-however-early-or-late-you-book) above.

### What information do you need from me to send a quote?

Your event date, the venue location, your expected guest count, and which package interests you. Those 4 details let us confirm equipment and technician availability in one exchange. See [What We Need From You](#what-we-need-from-you-to-build-an-accurate-quote) above.

### Can I add equipment or technician hours after I have already booked?

Yes, an add on request is possible, but it still has to clear the same 24 hour minimum notice as a first booking, and it is confirmed against whatever equipment or technician time is actually still available for your date, not guaranteed on request. See [The One Hard Deadline](#the-one-hard-deadline-24-hours-not-a-suggested-lead-time) above.

### Is there a deposit or contract before my date is secured?

We do not publish a deposit or contract policy for AV equipment. Your date is confirmed through the same 4 step process described above, quote request, our team finalizing details, and confirmation, not a separate deposit or signed contract step. If a specific arrangement matters to your planning, ask us directly at the quote stage.

### What is the minimum notice period for a booking or a change?

24 hours, for any event gear rental or technical service, and for any change to a booking already made. There is no shorter or longer version of this rule for larger or smaller events. See [The One Hard Deadline](#the-one-hard-deadline-24-hours-not-a-suggested-lead-time) above.
